TC08 Backplane
<UL>
<LI><b>tc083-18</b> is a 3-18-2004 checkpoint of TC08 drawing in progress.</LI>
<LI><b>indicators</b> is an LED version of the TC08 Indicator panel.</LI>
<LI><b>so-indicators</b> is a surface mount version of the indicators
board.</LI>
<LI><b>so-indicators-ok</b> is a backup of so-indicators.</LI>
<LI><b>tc08ss</b> is an experiment with routing one layer at a time.</LI>
<LI><b>tc08nh</b> is a successful routing without screw holes.  (It also
lacks an NC layer.)</LI>
<LI><b>tc08ttl</b> is an aborted attempt to convert to a "big board"
TTL implementation.</LI>
<LI><b>tc08</b> is a drawing of DEC's TC08 DECtape Controller.</LI>
<LI><b>tc08-6u</b> is a drawing of DEC's TC08 DECtape Controller, drawn to fit in 6Uin a DEC rack.</LI>
<LI><b>tc08-8-07</b> is an 8/2007 checkpoint of the TC08 drawing.  This one
does have the hidden "NC" layer, to simplify routing and reduce spurious
error messages.</LI>
